id: pm-bukwmy
title: Reject repository-local test scratch roots before sandbox fixtures can mutate the real Git workspace
description: "Setting TMPDIR inside the checkout makes disposable test fixtures inherit the real Git root and ancestor tracker. Observed coverage fixtures replaced repository .gitattributes and .gitignore managed sections and invalidated no-Git assertions. The package-owned test runner must reject this configuration before starting build or Vitest, including symlink aliases of the checkout; external scratch roots remain supported."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-08T05:41:23.494Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-08T07:22:02.040Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-08T07:09:27.039Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-08T07:09:27.039Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Repository-local and symlink-aliased temporary roots fail before child execution with a clear remediation.; External temporary roots still run sandboxed test and coverage modes without changing real Git or tracker state.
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: Reject workspace-local temporary roots before child execution; use portable owned fixture paths; test both inherited build modes and require structured terminal defect evidence.
expected_result: Protect the real tracker and Git workspace while allowing external scratch roots in local and prebuilt CI execution.
actual_result: "All 95 linked tests pass with CI skip-build enabled, including 24 runner tests covering both explicit build modes. Production code retains the full local 100-percent coverage result; post-closure defect and static gates are required before the correction push."
